  "id": "acquired-response",
  "term": "acquired response",
  "definition": "An acquired response is a pattern of responding that has been learned through recent task experience, such as a choice or strategy that previously led to good outcomes. In psychology, the term is often used when describing the need to overcome that learned response after task demands change.",
